<title>USA: Baltimore Gas workers reject union.</title>
<headline>Baltimore Gas workers reject union.</headline>
<dateline>BALTIMORE 1996-12-20</dateline>
<text>
<p>Baltimore Gas and Electric Co said on Friday that 1,864 of approximately 2,500 employees rejected union representation by the International Brotherhood of Electrical Workers.</p>
<p>Baltimore Gas said the union had tried to organize employees for the past two years.</p>
<p>In a National Labor Relations Board-conducted election, 1,864 employees voted against the union and 790 supported representation, the utility said. Baltimore Gas said remaining union free gives it a competitive advantage in a utility marketplace that will soon be deregulated.</p>
<p>Representatives of the International Brotherhood of Electrical Workers were not immediately available for comment.</p>
</text>
